A-29B Community FLIR reference
==============================

Source: https://github.com/luizrenault/a-29b-community
Revision: 1f632f004e28ef13a5f3404528de4c3fc982a0e2
Author/project: Luiz Renault and the A-29B Community contributors.

The files listed in import-manifest.json are unmodified upstream files.
The complete FLIR directory and its command/display integration references
are retained for the standalone Alpha compatibility port. Adaptations belong
in Avionics/AMX, not in this reference snapshot.

The upstream README permits reuse of Lua aircraft systems in non-paid DCS
World modules. Its separate C++ reuse terms require a request for non-paid,
public open-source modules. The unmodified avSimplest.dll from the same
official revision is retained for private compatibility testing. This
snapshot does not grant additional binary redistribution permissions.

No A-29B entry point, flight model, installer, identity or external mod path
is executed by the Alpha runtime. Keeping reference files does not establish
native sensor or video approval.